1
00:01:28,237 --> 00:01:34,076
RYOTSU IN TRAINING

2
00:01:34,877 --> 00:01:36,579
Good morning!

3
00:01:39,382 --> 00:01:41,283
Don't be so scared!

4
00:01:41,651 --> 00:01:43,953
I wasn't expecting you to look like that!

5
00:01:44,186 --> 00:01:46,756
What happened to your hair, Ryo-chan?

6
00:01:47,490 --> 00:01:48,491
Hmph!

7
00:01:48,724 --> 00:01:50,326
The thing is...

8
00:01:50,559 --> 00:01:51,394
Huh?

9
00:01:52,895 --> 00:01:54,930
Ryotsu borrowed money from you, Superintendent?

10
00:01:55,131 --> 00:01:58,434
He asked me so seriously that I couldn't help but lend it to him.

11
00:01:58,634 --> 00:02:02,505
It's true that there's a memorial service next week, but I'm not inviting Ryotsu.

12
00:02:02,738 --> 00:02:04,106
How much did you lend him?

13
00:02:04,607 --> 00:02:06,308
It was about 70,000 yen.

14
00:02:06,742 --> 00:02:07,810
70,000 yen!

15
00:02:11,047 --> 00:02:13,315
Ouch! What the heck are you doing!

16
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:14,917
Ch-Chief!

17
00:02:15,117 --> 00:02:16,886
You greedy fool!

18
00:02:17,219 --> 00:02:18,087
That's cruel!

19
00:02:18,287 --> 00:02:21,657
Even if you're the chief, you can't suddenly smack me from behind!

20
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:23,692
Who invited you to the memorial?

21
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:27,963
Huh, what? Was I wrong? Maybe I misunderstood?

22
00:02:28,364 --> 00:02:31,333
I'd never invite you under any circumstances!

23
00:02:33,002 --> 00:02:35,938
Your tough love is harsher than usual today, Chief.

24
00:02:36,138 --> 00:02:40,076
Of course! How dare you trick the superintendent into lending you money!

25
00:02:40,276 --> 00:02:41,343
Trick the superintendent?

26
00:02:42,244 --> 00:02:44,980
So that's how you could buy this 70,000-yen model kit.

27
00:02:45,181 --> 00:02:45,815
What?!

28
00:02:46,015 --> 00:02:47,917
No, Chief! Don't get the wrong idea.

29
00:02:48,117 --> 00:02:53,022
I bought this with money I saved up gradually by working hard! I swear!

30
00:02:53,389 --> 00:02:54,123
Oh...?

31
00:02:54,457 --> 00:02:55,191
Sit down!

32
00:02:55,391 --> 00:02:58,027
Terai, hold his legs! Nakagawa, his arms!

33
00:02:58,527 --> 00:02:59,662
Yes, sir!

34
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,567
W-What are you doing?!

35
00:03:05,735 --> 00:03:06,802
Oh no, ouch, ouch!

36
00:03:07,002 --> 00:03:09,705
I've decided to send you to a temple, starting tomorrow!

37
00:03:09,939 --> 00:03:13,542
Train at the temple for ten days and get rid of your greed for money!

38
00:03:15,144 --> 00:03:16,212
That's what happened.

39
00:03:16,412 --> 00:03:18,748
Huh, you never change, do you, Ryo-chan?

40
00:03:28,724 --> 00:03:31,594
"SHOTENJI TEMPLE"

41
00:03:32,394 --> 00:03:35,898
So, I would appreciate your help.

42
00:03:36,499 --> 00:03:39,235
Hey, Ryotsu, you should ask properly, too.

43
00:03:39,435 --> 00:03:42,505
But it's not like I want to train here.

44
00:03:42,705 --> 00:03:43,773
Stop complaining!

45
00:03:44,774 --> 00:03:46,208
And what's in that bag?

46
00:03:46,408 --> 00:03:49,411
Oh, this is ten days' worth of underwear and other stuff.

47
00:03:49,612 --> 00:03:52,448
I can't sleep without my own pillow.

48
00:03:52,681 --> 00:03:54,917
You're not going on an Amazon expedition!

49
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:55,751
Show me!

50
00:04:00,523 --> 00:04:05,861
Do you think you can train while bringing all these worldly things?

51
00:04:06,061 --> 00:04:09,565
That's why I want to use them as a warning to myself,

52
00:04:09,765 --> 00:04:12,001
so that I don't get carried away when I see them.

53
00:04:12,201 --> 00:04:15,638
Shut up! Confiscated! The temple will keep them all!

54
00:04:15,871 --> 00:04:17,773
Fine. Hmph!

55
00:04:19,341 --> 00:04:21,610
Worldly desires are hard to cut off.

56
00:04:22,077 --> 00:04:24,947
&lt;i&gt;Nice, looks like I can&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;get them back anytime.&lt;/i&gt;

57
00:04:25,347 --> 00:04:26,382
Ryotsu-san?

58
00:04:26,582 --> 00:04:27,449
Y-Yes.

59
00:04:27,650 --> 00:04:31,453
In place of your worldly name, I give you the Buddhist name "Chinnen."

60
00:04:31,921 --> 00:04:32,788
Ch-Chinnen?

61
00:04:33,255 --> 00:04:35,124
Over to you, Sennen and Mannen.

62
00:04:35,357 --> 00:04:36,192
Yes.

63
00:04:36,425 --> 00:04:38,761
These two will be your mentors.

64
00:04:39,061 --> 00:04:40,663
Begin your training at once.

65
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:42,498
We appreciate your guidance.

66
00:04:42,731 --> 00:04:43,799
Come on, Ryotsu!

67
00:04:44,567 --> 00:04:45,601
He appreciates it too!

68
00:04:47,269 --> 00:04:49,138
"NOVICE MONKS' DORMITORY"

69
00:04:55,277 --> 00:04:58,380
We've been training for a week now.

70
00:04:58,581 --> 00:04:59,682
I'm Zannen.

71
00:04:59,915 --> 00:05:00,649
I'm Munen.

72
00:05:00,850 --> 00:05:01,817
Pleased to meet you.

73
00:05:02,284 --> 00:05:06,121
We're all gonna eat from the same pot. So let's get along.

74
00:05:06,322 --> 00:05:08,490
Just leave it all to me!

75
00:05:08,757 --> 00:05:09,692
Huh...

76
00:05:10,259 --> 00:05:13,762
Clear your head of evil thoughts and practice zazen with an empty mind.

77
00:05:13,963 --> 00:05:14,597
Begin!

78
00:05:31,513 --> 00:05:32,147
&lt;i&gt;Katsu!&lt;/i&gt;

79
00:05:32,681 --> 00:05:35,017
You were caught by evil thoughts, weren't you?

80
00:05:35,451 --> 00:05:36,652
How can you tell?

81
00:05:36,852 --> 00:05:38,621
With years of training,

82
00:05:38,821 --> 00:05:41,624
I can easily read the thoughts of someone like you.

83
00:05:41,824 --> 00:05:42,458
Hmph!

84
00:05:42,658 --> 00:05:43,425
&lt;i&gt;Katsu!&lt;/i&gt;

85
00:05:43,626 --> 00:05:46,695
You just thought "it's a lie anyway," didn't you?

86
00:05:46,896 --> 00:05:48,297
I didn't think that!

87
00:05:48,497 --> 00:05:50,132
Don't make things up!

88
00:05:50,699 --> 00:05:53,369
Watch your mouth! Reflect on your behavior!

89
00:05:55,437 --> 00:05:56,906
Hmm... not bad.

90
00:05:57,139 --> 00:05:58,874
Don't underestimate me!

91
00:06:03,846 --> 00:06:04,713
Damn it!

92
00:06:14,056 --> 00:06:14,823
Ouch!

93
00:06:15,024 --> 00:06:15,891
You jerk!

94
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:18,560
I can't breathe!

95
00:06:18,761 --> 00:06:20,362
-Oww, oww, oww! -Why you...!

96
00:06:20,562 --> 00:06:25,034
The monks here all know martial arts, so it's better not to resist.

97
00:06:25,234 --> 00:06:26,769
Damn it!

98
00:06:42,384 --> 00:06:43,185
Wake up!

99
00:06:43,919 --> 00:06:46,789
W-What the hell! I thought my heart was gonna stop!

100
00:06:47,156 --> 00:06:48,891
Stop whining and get changed!

101
00:06:49,091 --> 00:06:53,262
Zannen, clean up the main hall garden. Munen and Chinnen, the hallway.

102
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:59,034
Crap! So that's why they gave us a log pillow. It all makes sense now.

103
00:06:59,902 --> 00:07:00,736
Huh?

104
00:07:06,375 --> 00:07:07,943
It's so long.

105
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:10,879
It's really hard to clean up the hallway of this temple.

106
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:13,615
I can't even see the end.

107
00:07:15,551 --> 00:07:16,752
Wait, wait!

108
00:07:16,952 --> 00:07:19,888
If we do it like that, it'll take forever.

109
00:07:20,089 --> 00:07:20,989
But...

110
00:07:28,464 --> 00:07:32,901
If we spread the cloths across the entire width, we can finish in one go.

111
00:07:33,102 --> 00:07:35,671
You go that way, and I'll go this way.

112
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:39,141
B-But if we do this, we might be cursed...

113
00:07:39,375 --> 00:07:41,477
Of "curse" we won't! Don't let fear stop you!

114
00:07:41,677 --> 00:07:43,979
If we run, we'll be done in five minutes.

115
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:45,981
Let's go!

116
00:08:00,129 --> 00:08:01,797
What? You already finished?

117
00:08:02,264 --> 00:08:03,932
Yes, all done.

118
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:07,636
Don't be stupid. It hasn't even been five minutes since you started.

119
00:08:07,836 --> 00:08:09,638
And now we've finished it all.

120
00:08:09,938 --> 00:08:13,642
All right! If you say so, I'll go and check it out.

121
00:08:13,842 --> 00:08:17,279
But if you're lying, you'll face the consequences.

122
00:08:17,479 --> 00:08:18,680
No problem.

123
00:08:19,148 --> 00:08:19,982
Oh!

124
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:30,159
Right, time for breakfast.

125
00:08:30,959 --> 00:08:33,195
What? Is this all?

126
00:08:33,629 --> 00:08:35,197
It's just porridge and pickles!

127
00:08:35,597 --> 00:08:39,735
Temples serve vegetarian food, so they don't use meat or fish.

128
00:08:39,968 --> 00:08:42,538
Eating only veggies as if you were grasshoppers!

129
00:08:42,738 --> 00:08:44,807
How can you put up with this?

130
00:08:45,007 --> 00:08:47,743
It can't be helped. This is part of our training.

131
00:08:47,976 --> 00:08:49,478
Now, let's eat.

132
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,714
Oh!

133
00:08:52,915 --> 00:08:54,316
"SOY-BRAISED BEEF"

134
00:08:55,818 --> 00:08:59,455
I smuggled it in inside my underwear. You can have some too.

135
00:08:59,655 --> 00:09:00,489
No!

136
00:09:00,689 --> 00:09:03,025
Eating meat is forbidden!

137
00:09:03,225 --> 00:09:04,893
We'll be punished.

138
00:09:05,094 --> 00:09:05,727
Huh?

139
00:09:06,061 --> 00:09:09,031
Is that so? There's plenty more.

140
00:09:13,669 --> 00:09:17,539
If you guys don't want any, I'll eat them all by myself.

141
00:09:17,739 --> 00:09:18,774
Let's eat!

142
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:27,182
Oh, it's delicious. Are you sure you don't want any?

143
00:09:29,084 --> 00:09:29,918
I'll have some!

144
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:32,121
Mmm, it's delicious!

145
00:09:32,888 --> 00:09:35,891
That's right. Humans must be honest about their desires.

146
00:09:36,091 --> 00:09:39,128
You guys have got some potential. Huh?

147
00:09:42,865 --> 00:09:45,734
What are you guys doing?

148
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,275
My deepest apologies, Sennen-sama!

149
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,978
Zannen and Munen have done something outrageous.

150
00:09:56,211 --> 00:10:00,249
I tried my best to stop them, but they wouldn't listen to me.

151
00:10:00,449 --> 00:10:01,416
N-No way!

152
00:10:01,617 --> 00:10:02,918
These are Chinnen-san's...

153
00:10:03,118 --> 00:10:05,721
Shut up! And now you're blaming someone else!

154
00:10:06,121 --> 00:10:08,724
&lt;i&gt;Katsu!&lt;/i&gt; It's joint responsibility.

155
00:10:08,924 --> 00:10:10,893
Zazen in the hallway till night! Got it?

156
00:10:11,226 --> 00:10:12,728
Oh no...

157
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:19,835
&lt;i&gt;Katsu!&lt;/i&gt;

158
00:10:27,609 --> 00:10:28,443
Ow, ow, ow...

159
00:10:28,644 --> 00:10:29,912
Ugh!

160
00:10:30,112 --> 00:10:32,114
My legs are completely stiff!

161
00:10:32,314 --> 00:10:34,650
Is there really nothing to do but zazen?

162
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:36,318
"NOVICE MONKS' DORMITORY"

163
00:10:36,718 --> 00:10:40,389
No radio, no TV, no manga, nothing.

164
00:10:40,589 --> 00:10:43,492
Boring, nothing to do but sleep.

165
00:10:43,725 --> 00:10:44,660
This sucks!

166
00:10:44,927 --> 00:10:46,795
Sleep early, or tomorrow will be tough.

167
00:10:49,097 --> 00:10:50,799
I'm too hungry to sleep!

168
00:10:50,999 --> 00:10:52,401
Let's order sushi delivery!

169
00:10:52,968 --> 00:10:54,503
That's impossible.

170
00:10:54,736 --> 00:10:58,507
Even if we could, it wouldn't be delivered to this temple.

171
00:10:58,740 --> 00:10:59,875
Security is too strict.

172
00:11:00,275 --> 00:11:02,844
Then, we'll just go out to eat.

173
00:11:05,113 --> 00:11:06,014
You can't do that!

174
00:11:06,215 --> 00:11:07,983
It'll be fine. It's nighttime.

175
00:11:15,324 --> 00:11:17,593
If I can just get out of here, I'll be almost there...

176
00:11:23,298 --> 00:11:24,533
W-What?

177
00:11:24,766 --> 00:11:27,769
A cat? A really big cat.

178
00:11:28,604 --> 00:11:30,372
N-No way...

179
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:37,546
Damn! What kind of temple is this?!

180
00:11:44,653 --> 00:11:46,788
Heh, you can't get me here.

181
00:11:50,025 --> 00:11:51,893
Argh! Piranhas!

182
00:11:55,263 --> 00:11:56,898
C-C-Crocodile!

183
00:12:04,573 --> 00:12:05,407
Hey, Chinnen!

184
00:12:08,744 --> 00:12:09,845
There's no escape!

185
00:12:10,112 --> 00:12:11,513
Never mind that.

186
00:12:12,581 --> 00:12:15,017
Do something about these animals!

187
00:12:26,561 --> 00:12:28,130
Is Ryo-san not here?

188
00:12:28,730 --> 00:12:31,933
I came all the way here to ask about strategies for this game.

189
00:12:32,367 --> 00:12:35,570
I'm sorry. Ryo-chan is now in training.

190
00:12:35,771 --> 00:12:36,605
Darn...

191
00:12:37,539 --> 00:12:39,908
Ryo-chan is surprisingly popular.

192
00:12:40,108 --> 00:12:46,381
Since yesterday, kids keep coming, asking for toy repairs and game tips.

193
00:12:46,982 --> 00:12:49,284
Ryotsu is very good at those kinds of things.

194
00:12:49,518 --> 00:12:50,686
That's true.

195
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,956
I wonder how he's doing now.

196
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,597
Right, I'll leave the rest to you.

197
00:13:03,332 --> 00:13:04,299
Have a nice day.

198
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:06,568
Oh, have a nice day.

199
00:13:07,302 --> 00:13:08,570
What happened?

200
00:13:08,970 --> 00:13:11,973
I heard some important monk passed away.

201
00:13:12,174 --> 00:13:14,776
Apparently, abbots from all over Tokyo will gather.

202
00:13:14,976 --> 00:13:17,646
Yay! Then, it's just us today!

203
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:21,783
Twist, twist, no zazen...

204
00:13:21,983 --> 00:13:24,886
But we have to continue training properly.

205
00:13:26,755 --> 00:13:27,589
Now is the time.

206
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:29,758
This is it.

207
00:13:36,264 --> 00:13:38,300
My RC car turned out to be unexpectedly useful.

208
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:40,802
I can mop the floor and have fun at the same time!

209
00:13:41,002 --> 00:13:42,671
I should have done this from the start.

210
00:13:43,105 --> 00:13:44,673
Oh no! This is serious!

211
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:48,176
What's going on?

212
00:13:48,844 --> 00:13:51,012
There's a memorial service today at 10 a.m.!

213
00:13:51,213 --> 00:13:53,181
I thought it was tomorrow.

214
00:13:53,382 --> 00:13:54,649
What?!

215
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:57,853
Why didn't you tell the abbot such an important thing!

216
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:00,689
Oh, what should I do? This is all my fault!

217
00:14:01,022 --> 00:14:02,057
I'll let him know!

218
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:03,625
Hey, wait a second!

219
00:14:03,825 --> 00:14:07,929
I don't want to sit on my legs all day again as joint responsibility.

220
00:14:08,663 --> 00:14:10,632
I'll go as the acting abbot.

221
00:14:10,966 --> 00:14:11,867
Chinnen-san?

222
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:13,468
Are you sure?

223
00:14:13,835 --> 00:14:16,772
Well, I'm pretty good at bluffing.

224
00:14:16,972 --> 00:14:17,806
Leave it to me.

225
00:14:23,145 --> 00:14:25,347
What do you think? I look like an abbot, right?

226
00:14:25,547 --> 00:14:27,048
Well, I guess so.

227
00:14:27,482 --> 00:14:28,884
Then, I'll go.

228
00:14:29,084 --> 00:14:30,152
Have a nice day.

229
00:14:41,963 --> 00:14:44,666
"SECOND ANNIVERSARY MEMORIAL FOR YAKUZA BOSS KUNIMITSU OKI"

230
00:14:48,003 --> 00:14:50,405
This is bad! If I get caught, I'll be killed.

231
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:51,873
Welcome, Abbot.

232
00:14:57,279 --> 00:14:59,047
This way, please.

233
00:14:59,247 --> 00:15:00,215
Y-Yes!

234
00:15:14,896 --> 00:15:16,932
&lt;i&gt;Damn, there's no turning back!&lt;/i&gt;

235
00:15:17,299 --> 00:15:22,370
Uh, Namu Ami, Amen, Eloim Essaim,

236
00:15:23,305 --> 00:15:26,408
Yaren, Soren, Kita Senju,

237
00:15:26,608 --> 00:15:29,778
Ayase, Kameari, Kanemachi,

238
00:15:30,011 --> 00:15:35,150
Matsudo, Ryogoku, Asakusa, Akihabara.

239
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:36,551
That's all.

240
00:15:36,751 --> 00:15:37,586
Uh-oh...

241
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,254
Abbot!

242
00:15:39,454 --> 00:15:40,489
&lt;i&gt;Oh no, they found out!&lt;/i&gt;

243
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:43,458
I'm so moved!

244
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:45,460
Your sutra spoke to us!

245
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:46,495
Yes, yes!

246
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:47,729
Eh?

247
00:15:48,497 --> 00:15:50,065
Thank you very much!

248
00:15:50,632 --> 00:15:51,800
Not at all.

249
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:53,468
Well then, Amen, da-butsu

250
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:55,737
Here. A small token of our thanks.

251
00:16:07,315 --> 00:16:08,650
I got through it somehow.

252
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:13,488
Sutra books are full of Chinese characters and no use for amateurs.

253
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:15,657
Anyway, how much did they give me?

254
00:16:16,124 --> 00:16:18,660
Wow! That's amazing!

255
00:16:19,327 --> 00:16:22,731
I didn't know I could get that much for just one memorial service.

256
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:27,002
Welcome back. How was it?

257
00:16:27,469 --> 00:16:30,772
Oh, perfect! I recited a sacred sutra!

258
00:16:31,072 --> 00:16:32,107
That's great.

259
00:16:32,307 --> 00:16:34,743
Now, let's have some fun!

260
00:16:34,943 --> 00:16:39,848
Order assorted sashimi and sukiyaki meat for 10 people.

261
00:16:40,081 --> 00:16:42,384
Let's have a party before the head monks get back!

262
00:16:42,617 --> 00:16:44,519
B-But the cost...

263
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:45,554
Idiot!

264
00:16:45,787 --> 00:16:49,324
A would-be monk shouldn't think such a worldly thing!

265
00:16:49,524 --> 00:16:50,992
Y-Yes...

266
00:16:51,192 --> 00:16:53,461
Worldly things are no good.

267
00:16:54,129 --> 00:16:57,465
Order two cases of beer from the liquor store, too.

268
00:17:03,939 --> 00:17:05,574
Cheers!

269
00:17:10,345 --> 00:17:12,380
I'm spinning them more than usual.

270
00:17:12,781 --> 00:17:13,682
Ha! That's great!

271
00:17:13,882 --> 00:17:15,517
Nice one, Chinnen-san!

272
00:17:17,252 --> 00:17:18,653
A phone call.

273
00:17:18,987 --> 00:17:20,855
Red Snake, come on!

274
00:17:21,056 --> 00:17:23,258
Here, Kiss of Fire!

275
00:17:23,491 --> 00:17:26,061
Hey, Yellow! Why don't you come out?

276
00:17:26,528 --> 00:17:27,729
How could I do that?!

277
00:17:29,064 --> 00:17:30,398
You're so funny, Chinnen-san!

278
00:17:31,399 --> 00:17:32,801
Okay, your turn. Do something.

279
00:17:33,001 --> 00:17:33,902
Me?

280
00:17:34,135 --> 00:17:38,573
You'll never become a good monk if you can't even do one party trick.

281
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,542
Oh no! Oh no!

282
00:17:41,242 --> 00:17:42,844
What? Another problem?

283
00:17:43,178 --> 00:17:44,813
Chinnen-san, the phone call...

284
00:17:45,013 --> 00:17:46,881
Call me Abbot Chinnen.

285
00:17:47,082 --> 00:17:49,384
Um, Abbot Chinnen.

286
00:17:49,584 --> 00:17:54,422
The abbot's brother says he can't attend a memorial service due to a cold

287
00:17:54,623 --> 00:17:56,891
and asks if the abbot can go in his place.

288
00:17:57,092 --> 00:17:57,926
All right.

289
00:17:58,159 --> 00:18:00,195
Tell him I'll go.

290
00:18:00,395 --> 00:18:01,363
Oh, okay.

291
00:18:01,563 --> 00:18:04,099
Abbot Chinnen, are you sure?

292
00:18:04,299 --> 00:18:07,702
Leave it to me! If you refuse a memorial service, you'll be punished.

293
00:18:07,902 --> 00:18:10,605
You must never go against the path of the Buddha.

294
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:11,940
Y-You're right.

295
00:18:12,173 --> 00:18:14,409
Everything is part of our training.

296
00:18:14,609 --> 00:18:16,044
You guys, come along too.

297
00:18:16,378 --> 00:18:19,247
Yay! I wonder how much I'll get this time!

298
00:18:19,447 --> 00:18:20,482
Wait for us!

299
00:18:32,293 --> 00:18:33,294
Hmm...

300
00:18:34,062 --> 00:18:37,232
Ah, found it. This is the place, Abbot Chinnen.

301
00:18:40,268 --> 00:18:41,603
"OHARA"

302
00:18:47,642 --> 00:18:49,310
What! Why is the chief here?

303
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:52,681
Oh, Abbot, we've been waiting for you.

304
00:18:53,448 --> 00:18:56,217
&lt;i&gt;Oh no, this is the chief's&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;brother's house.&lt;/i&gt;

305
00:18:56,685 --> 00:18:58,820
I'm sorry. I know you're busy.

306
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:00,755
Actually, I have an urgent...

307
00:19:00,955 --> 00:19:01,623
Hey!

308
00:19:01,823 --> 00:19:02,991
Listen, come on!

309
00:19:03,291 --> 00:19:04,459
This is my brother.

310
00:19:04,659 --> 00:19:05,493
Hello.

311
00:19:05,694 --> 00:19:08,463
This is the monk who has come as the acting abbot.

312
00:19:09,064 --> 00:19:10,532
Thank you for having me.

313
00:19:10,765 --> 00:19:12,500
Thank you for coming.

314
00:19:13,501 --> 00:19:14,769
Huh?

315
00:19:14,969 --> 00:19:16,771
Well, see you later.

316
00:19:21,676 --> 00:19:22,811
Huh...

317
00:19:23,778 --> 00:19:26,247
-Yoshida had a baby. -Really?

318
00:19:27,782 --> 00:19:29,484
I prepared for 22 people...

319
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,853
Looks like we can't escape.

320
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:32,854
Oh!

321
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:33,688
What's up?

322
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:38,860
I was in a rush, and mixed up the bag with our hoods with the one with party stuff...

323
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:40,128
What!

324
00:19:40,328 --> 00:19:41,563
You got the wrong one?

325
00:19:41,796 --> 00:19:43,498
But there's no turning back now.

326
00:19:43,698 --> 00:19:45,533
We'll have to get away with it somehow!

327
00:19:45,734 --> 00:19:46,367
Yes!

328
00:20:06,054 --> 00:20:07,322
What on earth is this?

329
00:20:08,757 --> 00:20:10,191
L-Looks like him!

330
00:20:10,391 --> 00:20:11,025
Huh?

331
00:20:11,326 --> 00:20:12,494
Please be quiet.

332
00:20:15,597 --> 00:20:18,166
Well, even though we belong to the same sect,

333
00:20:18,366 --> 00:20:21,536
our practices may differ slightly. Please understand.

334
00:20:21,736 --> 00:20:25,240
You may find our sutra chanting faster than usual,

335
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:28,042
but each word carries deep meaning.

336
00:20:28,376 --> 00:20:29,244
Ahem.

337
00:20:29,511 --> 00:20:31,312
Namu...

338
00:20:35,517 --> 00:20:36,584
That's all.

339
00:20:36,918 --> 00:20:38,019
What?

340
00:20:39,888 --> 00:20:41,623
Does that man really look like him?

341
00:20:41,856 --> 00:20:43,858
Yes, his name is Ryotsu,

342
00:20:44,058 --> 00:20:46,060
and he's a hopeless idiot.

343
00:20:46,861 --> 00:20:47,695
Hmm?

344
00:20:48,363 --> 00:20:51,332
All right, today I'm going to give you a special treat.

345
00:20:51,533 --> 00:20:53,468
The sutra continues.

346
00:20:53,701 --> 00:20:56,104
Hey, you there, I need a little help.

347
00:20:56,571 --> 00:20:57,739
Huh?

348
00:20:58,072 --> 00:21:01,943
When I chant, I need you to spin around three times and bark.

349
00:21:02,243 --> 00:21:03,578
Eh? What for?

350
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:06,080
I told you our sect has different customs.

351
00:21:06,281 --> 00:21:08,583
Do it, or you'll be punished.

352
00:21:09,217 --> 00:21:10,652
Do as you're told!

353
00:21:10,885 --> 00:21:11,953
But, brother!

354
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,188
Just do it!

355
00:21:17,091 --> 00:21:18,259
All right, here we go.

356
00:21:18,459 --> 00:21:22,263
Namu...

357
00:21:22,463 --> 00:21:23,097
Woof!

358
00:21:23,298 --> 00:21:23,965
No!

359
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:28,970
Open your mouth wider, drool a little, then bark!

360
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:30,238
Got it?

361
00:21:30,438 --> 00:21:31,606
No way...

362
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,475
You must not resist!

363
00:21:34,809 --> 00:21:36,244
That hurts!

364
00:21:36,444 --> 00:21:38,646
Clear your mind, and pain will disappear.

365
00:21:38,846 --> 00:21:41,316
It's nothing compared to being hit with a bamboo sword.

366
00:21:41,516 --> 00:21:42,317
Eh?

367
00:21:42,984 --> 00:21:45,853
Oh, you remembered something, didn't you?

368
00:21:46,087 --> 00:21:48,489
Did you hit your poor subordinate with a bamboo sword?

369
00:21:48,690 --> 00:21:52,527
If you don't confess honestly, everyone here will be punished!

370
00:21:55,864 --> 00:21:58,066
Well, you remember doing it, don't you?

371
00:22:00,268 --> 00:22:01,669
What do you say, Daijiro?

372
00:22:01,870 --> 00:22:02,537
Ah, yes.

373
00:22:03,004 --> 00:22:04,639
How terrifying!

374
00:22:04,839 --> 00:22:07,709
Because of this man, divine punishment may befall us all!

375
00:22:10,445 --> 00:22:11,879
Daijiro, apologize!

376
00:22:12,113 --> 00:22:15,984
If you repent in front of the great monk from Shotenji Temple, you'll be forgiven.

377
00:22:16,184 --> 00:22:16,851
Huh?

378
00:22:17,185 --> 00:22:18,620
Shotenji Temple?

379
00:22:20,989 --> 00:22:24,626
Excuse me, but would you take off those nose glasses?

380
00:22:24,826 --> 00:22:26,427
W-What are you talking about?

381
00:22:26,628 --> 00:22:29,130
This is a characteristic of our sect.

382
00:22:29,330 --> 00:22:30,431
Absolutely not!

383
00:22:30,632 --> 00:22:31,666
Oh?

384
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,969
Are you not listening to me?

385
00:22:35,169 --> 00:22:37,105
I'll curse you for seven generations!

386
00:22:37,305 --> 00:22:38,306
Hmm...

387
00:22:38,506 --> 00:22:40,208
Hey, Daijiro.

388
00:22:40,441 --> 00:22:42,644
Ryotsu, there's 10,000 yen on the floor.

389
00:22:42,844 --> 00:22:45,680
Where is it? Where?

390
00:22:50,551 --> 00:22:51,819
I got you!

391
00:22:52,020 --> 00:22:53,821
This guy is Ryotsu in disguise!

392
00:22:54,222 --> 00:22:56,324
No, that's some kind of misunderstanding...

393
00:22:56,524 --> 00:22:57,392
Ryotsu!

394
00:22:58,226 --> 00:22:59,560
Get back here!

395
00:22:59,761 --> 00:23:02,730
Stop it! How could you do that to a revered monk?

396
00:23:02,931 --> 00:23:04,732
Someone, stop this man!

397
00:23:08,036 --> 00:23:09,003
Ohhh!

398
00:23:12,173 --> 00:23:14,242
Ch-Chief, there's a reason for this...

399
00:23:14,475 --> 00:23:16,944
Shut up! I don't care about any reason!

400
00:23:17,178 --> 00:23:18,713
Go to hell!

401
00:23:18,913 --> 00:23:21,249
Please stop, Chief!

402
00:23:23,851 --> 00:23:27,388
Apparently he also had parties with sashimi and sukiyaki at the temple.

403
00:23:27,755 --> 00:23:29,857
That's so typical of Ryo-chan.

404
00:23:30,058 --> 00:23:31,926
So, what about his training?

405
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:35,897
He'll stay at the temple for life until he truly reflects.

406
00:23:37,365 --> 00:23:39,267
D-Don't come closer! Go away!

407
00:23:39,867 --> 00:23:42,070
Not me! It's these guys who are bad!

408
00:23:42,270 --> 00:23:44,072
If you're hungry, eat them!

409
00:23:45,206 --> 00:23:47,775
If you clear your mind, even fire feels cool.

410
00:23:47,975 --> 00:23:49,811
And even a lion becomes a cat.

411
00:23:50,044 --> 00:23:52,780
You need more training, Chinnen-san.

412
00:23:57,051 --> 00:23:59,754
H-Help me!

413
00:24:03,191 --> 00:24:09,030
AH, MY HOME
